bump this file to build Seance on Brandon's Mac (and install it there)
build 1: SEANCE - twelve spirits round a table on the Six Sines engine widened to twelve operators (66 links, 12 feedbacks). Drag a spirit onto a higher-numbered one = it possesses it; click a spirit, a thread or the middle for its panel; every Six Sines / Poltergeist 2 factory sound loads into seats 1-6. VST3 + CLAP. Not yet: wavetable and Surge species, backward links, FX / SUB / MORPH pages
build 2: any spirit can possess any other now (132 links; a higher seat onto a lower one arrives one engine block late), both directions of a pair at once, loops allowed. FX page (the spectral rack: four slots + the inversion) and SUB page (the sub-bass, 8 sounds) over the table, both off until you turn them on. The DAW's parameter list shows only ON and DEPTH for the 117 new links
build 3: BEASTS - any seat can be one of Surge XT's own oscillators (Classic, Modern, String, Twist, Alias, Noise, FM2, FM3): SPECIES on the spirit panel, its own seven knobs under BODY, horns on the table. A beast takes the same threads, feedback, ratio and envelopes as a sine spirit, and can possess others. Surge is built on its own and linked in behind a small door (src/ghostblock/beast), its code untouched
build 4: THROAT - every spirit can sing through one of Surge XT's own filters (214 of them: ladders, OB-Xd, K35, diode, warps, tri-pole, state-variable ...) on its own output, before anything hears it: THROAT tab on the spirit panel (pick the filter, CUTOFF, RESONANCE, KEYTRACK), a collar on the spirit. Also everything of build 3 (the beasts), which never reached the Mac: its runner lost contact mid-build, so the build now keeps the Mac awake and leaves one core free
build 5: SHADES - any seat can be Vital's wavetable oscillator (SPECIES = Wavetable): eight wavetables of our own, FRAME to move through a table, nine of Vital's spectral morphs, six of its warps (sync, formant, quantize, bend, squeeze, pulse width), unison up to 16, all under BODY; a crown of waves on the table. A shade takes threads as phase modulation with no delay, has feedback, and can possess others. Heavy: about 1.7 % of a core per sounding shade voice here. Also builds 3 and 4 (beasts, THROAT), which have not reached the Mac yet
build 5b: the same as build 5, queued again (build 5 never left the queue)
build 5c: the beasts (Surge oscillators) were left out of 5b: their build script tripped on the Mac's older shell before compiling anything. Fixed; this build should carry sine spirits, beasts, shades and throats together
build 5d: the beasts compiled and passed their own checks on the Mac in 5c, but the last step (packing Surge's engine into one object) was refused because the door's names were hidden. Fixed
build 5e: 5d packed Surge's engine, but two stray C names inside it were still visible and the build's own leak check stopped it. They are hidden now
build 5f: this Mac's linker has no switch to hide those two names; they are harmless (two empty C variables), so the leak check allows them
build 6: a shade can play the Vital wavetable files on this Mac. On a shade spirit, TABLE (top right, where WAVE is on a sine spirit) lists every .vitaltable in Music/Vital by pack, Factory first; the file is read where it is and built by Vital's own wavetable code (all 19 factory tables checked). The table is saved inside the sound, FRAME moves through it, and the TABLE knob greys while a file is loaded
build 7: 16 new factory sounds made for Seance (folders "Seance Bass / Bells / Pads / Leads / Keys / Effects") using sine spirits, beasts, shades and throats; and 13 sounds on your own Vital factory wavetables, written on your Mac into YOUR SOUNDS > Vital Tables. Each was played through the engine and level-trimmed before it was written; nobody has listened to them yet
build 8: MOVE - a new tab on every spirit. Its own LFO (RATE, SHAPE) and its PITCH envelope can sweep its filter's cutoff (LFO > CUTOFF, ENV > CUTOFF) and, on a wavetable spirit, FRAME, MORPH or WARP (pick with MOVES), separately for every note. Sweeps with nothing to sweep are greyed. 8 of the Seance sounds and 9 of the Vital-table sounds now move
build 9: a wavetable spirit can load ordinary .wav wavetables (Serum-style: one cycle after another) - TABLE FILE > "Load a .wav wavetable...". It is saved inside the sound and FRAME moves through it like any other table. The FX page's knobs, switches and menus are now drawn like the rest of Seance
build 10: a sound now opens exactly the way it was saved - the FX page and the SUB page are stored inside the sound and come back with it. A sound saved without them (the factory sounds, NEW) turns them off. Sounds saved before this build have no FX stored: open one, set its FX again and SAVE it once
build 11: a new folder of ten sounds, "Seance Twelve", where all twelve spirits are in use and connected: The Long Chain, Six Marriages, Coven Choir, Three Towers, Cathedral, Ouroboros, Beast Parliament, Legion, Twelve Drawbars, Wraith Swarm. Each was played through the engine and level-trimmed; nobody has listened to them yet
build 12: CROSS - a new page (top right, after SUB): four sounds at four corners and a flame you drag between them; you hear a blend of the real sounds, each played by its own engine. Any corner can be the sound on the table, a frozen copy of it, a factory sound or one of yours; each has VOLUME, PAN and OCTAVE; ORBIT makes the flame circle in time with the song. Also: on a Surge spirit the MOVE tab can now sweep that oscillator's own knobs (pick which with MOVES)
build 13: SUMMON - a new button in the top bar. Pick a character (a bass, a bell, a pad, a lead, keys, or "something unholy") and it makes a brand-new sound: decides which spirits sing and which possess which, picks wavetables, Surge oscillators, filters and movement, plays it to itself, sets the level, and names it. Every press is a different sound. It is not kept until you SAVE it
build 14: HANDS and MACROS. Every spirit has a new tab, HANDS: its volume, feedback and pitch can each follow how you play (velocity, the mod wheel, aftertouch, pitch bend, how high the note is, a random value per note) or one of six MACRO knobs, with an amount. Every thread has DEPTH FOLLOWS the same way. The six macro knobs are in the circle's panel (click the middle of the table, then MACROS). Controls that have nothing to push are greyed
build 15: the SUMMON menu can now also MUTATE the sound on the table (a little, or a lot) - same sound, nudged: depths, ratios, wavetable positions, filters and tails drift, and it is re-levelled. "Bring back the sound before that" undoes the last SUMMON or MUTATE. Summoned sounds now often get brighter the harder you play
build 16: STEPS - a sequencer page (top right, after CROSS). Turn it on and the keys you play drive it. PATTERN menu: MIDNIGHT and DUSK from ArpEZator's own engine - "a new idea" writes chords, arp, melody and bass and one held key plays it in that key (ARP and MELODY start on; CHORDS and BASS are a click away), "a new arp figure" plays that mood's arp over whatever chord you hold; ANOTHER writes a new one. Plus 14 one-key lines (octave pump, acid crawl, tresillo, trance gate ...) and 14 held-chord arps (up, down, thumb pedal, converge ...), or draw your own in the grid. SPEED, OCTAVE, LATCH, LENGTH, SWING. Follows the song's tempo and beat. Saved with the project and inside a sound
build 17: STEPS grid grows up - drag a note to move it, drag its right end for length, mouse wheel for loudness, right-click a note or a bar for more (octave, which part, copy a bar, clear); DRAW ON picks the part; LOOP sets 1-16 bars; DRAG MIDI OUT drops the pattern into the piano roll. STEPS also gets SUNRISE, TRAP and HIP HOP from ArpEZator. SUMMON can use your Vital wavetables, "Change only..." mutates one thing (depths, tuning, wavetables, filters, envelopes), "New voices" swaps the oscillators and keeps the rest. Every FOLLOWS has a second slot beside it. Macros can be named. New folder "Seance Played": ten sounds that use velocity, the mod wheel, macros and STEPS
build 18: a level meter under VOICES with a safety limiter behind it (click the meter to switch the limiter off or on; on by default) so loud sounds cannot clip. STEPS ideas get CHORDS: YOURS - the MIDNIGHT / DUSK / SUNRISE / TRAP / HIP HOP idea is re-written over whatever chord you hold and follows your changes. Right-click a note > set its loudness and length exactly. SUMMON > Summon around this sound (keep the wiring, the voices or the envelopes; the rest is new). The sound list has FIND A SOUND and FAVOURITES. STEPS switches and the limiter can be automated from FL (the CROSS flame already could). Seven comb filters at the end of the THROAT menu
build 19: a new Seance now opens on the factory sound "A Supporting Role" (Bass folder) in place of the plain starting sound. Projects you already saved open with their own sound as before; NEW still gives the plain one
build 20: CROSSROADS - a menu on the CROSS page with 12 ready-made blends: Low End Council, Reese Rising, Glass Into Choir, Night Keys, Lead Shapeshifter, Slow Weather, Coven of Twelve, Bell Garden, Bowed Light, Organ Loft, Supersaw Dawn, Weight and Air. Each puts four sounds that sit together in the corners, level-matched so moving the flame changes the sound and not the volume, with the orbit set to move it for you. "Save this crossroads" keeps your own under YOURS
build 21: the CROSS page now catches corners cancelling each other. A readout under the corner panels says BLEND: CLEAN or CANCELLING x dB. FIX CANCELLING (on by default) turns a corner that fights the others upside down so it adds instead, and keeps the blend at a steady level while the flame moves. Switch it off to hear the plain mix
